EXTENSION "ARMDef_The_Sundered_Eagle_TheIslands_MemnosOfHouseVerditius" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Sundered Eagle - Memnos of House Verditius"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_The_Sundered_Eagle_Core_Ext"

    # Memnos of House Verditius (Chapter Six: The Islands, p85): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t65e1b77a77d6e8d2aee121 ^"Memnos of House Verditius" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t99d78701a695218b339395 ^"Favonius"]
            ^"Age" STRING "92 (Apparent Age: 58)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Hubris +4, Fearful of Open Water +3, Diligent +2, Talkative –2"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Sundered Eagle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 85
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Memnos is the founder of the covenant and architect of its marvelous vessels. He is a member of the Mystic Fraternity of Samos (*The Mysteries Revised Edition* pages 126 –129); or, if your saga does not include this Mystery Cult, a suitable alternative that teaches Hermetic Architecture. He has always been fascinated with ships and boats, and is specialized in their enchantment. However, an unfortunate incident during a Mystery Initiation left him with a Death Prophecy that he would die “with the sky above him and the sea beneath him”. He has never actually sailed on any of his ships for fear of the prophecy’s completion. He has become famed as a builder of sea-going vessels and is nearly always busy working on one commission or another.\n\nMemnos is a healthy man apparently in his fifties, with curly black hair and a full beard. His skin has turned nut-brown from his outdoors life on the seashore. His work with hefty beams of wood has left him massively muscled, and he is an expert climber with a good sense of balance. He is best skilled in the Art of Rego, and is particularly accomplished in craft magic, which he uses to lighten his work. He has a team of 4 forge-companions (see *Houses of Hermes: Mystery Cults*, page 113), and his laboratory on Andros contains many specializations and enhancements."
    }

}
